.TH "SKOGAI RUNNER-WO" 1  "skogai runner-wo 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai runner\-wo \- workorders: one bounded question, gathered inputs, checkable output
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai runner wo\fR <COMMAND>
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skogai runner\-wo\-new(1)
scaffold a workorder
.TP
skogai runner\-wo\-run(1)
run a workorder, write <name>.result.json beside it

with \-\-sandbox (or `sandbox: true` in the workorder) the worker runs in a
fresh `skogai module sandbox` at .skogai/tmp/sandbox/<name>: its cwd is the
sandbox repo, its skogai config is the sandbox's, every module found from
here is installed there. the sandbox is kept for a look afterwards.
.TP
skogai runner\-wo\-ls(1)
list workorders and whether they have a result
